# Tests for the `mathdemo` module.

fiveFactorialTest is test
fiveFactorialTest purpose "The factorial of 5 is computed as 120"
fiveFactorialTest verifies factorial fiveFactorial
fiveFactorialTest typeParameter none
fiveFactorialTest input none
fiveFactorialTest output none
fiveFactorialTest outputOwnedBy none
fiveFactorialTest raises none
fiveFactorialTest effect none
fiveFactorialTest uses none
fiveFactorialTest memoryHeap false
fiveFactorialTest async false
fiveFactorialTest maxRecursion none
fiveFactorialTest label begin loopKind none
fiveFactorialTest label begin within none
fiveFactorialTest let five Int64 5 immutable
fiveFactorialTest let expected Int64 120 immutable
fiveFactorialTest at begin do computeFive
fiveFactorialTest at begin do expectOneHundredTwenty
fiveFactorialTest at begin return ok none

computeFive is call
computeFive in fiveFactorialTest
computeFive invokes factorial
computeFive argument n Int64 five copy
computeFive result actual Int64
computeFive ownedBy none
computeFive cleanedBy none
computeFive borrows none
computeFive catch none

expectOneHundredTwenty is call
expectOneHundredTwenty in fiveFactorialTest
expectOneHundredTwenty invokes test.assertEqualInt64
expectOneHundredTwenty argument expected Int64 expected copy
expectOneHundredTwenty argument actual Int64 actual copy
expectOneHundredTwenty result none
expectOneHundredTwenty ownedBy none
expectOneHundredTwenty cleanedBy none
expectOneHundredTwenty borrows none
expectOneHundredTwenty catch none
